And you look at that, that's not
an obvious choice, is it?

295
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,680
两人：确实想不到。
- 要是想把孩子放在安全的地方，
BOTH: No.
- If you wanted to put
children somewhere safe,

296
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,520
你肯定会选沃尔沃、奔驰或者大号四驱车。
you'd go Volvo or Mercedes or a big 4x4.

297
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,960
但偏偏是那辆车脱颖而出，
But that is actually singled out

298
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,520
装上儿童座椅后
表现极其拔尖，
with its child seats
as being very, very good

299
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,960
不管是侧面碰撞还是正面碰撞。
in both side impacts and frontal ones.

300
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,240
事情就是这样。
So there we are.

301
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,720
好。有人留意到
Right. Has anybody seen

302
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:57,520
那位交通大臣阿利斯泰尔·达林了吗？真是难为他了。
that Transport Minister
Alistair Darling? Bless him.

303
00:12:57,560 --> 00:13:00,800
他一直在嚷嚷
说我们需要设立一位“路坑沙皇”。
He's been saying
that we need is a "Hole Tsar."

304
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,640
什么玩意儿？
- 因为马路上到处都是坑……
A what?
- Because of all the holes in the road...

305
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:04,880
主要是因为各部门毫无规划、一团混乱，
It's because of all the disorganisation,

306
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:08,200
我记得是在伦敦河岸街，居然挖了大概160个坑……
I think it was in London on
the Strand about 160 holes...

307
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,280
就在12个月之内，没错。
In 12 months, yeah.

308
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:12,440
全无统筹。结果就是：
交通瘫痪、大堵车、乱成一锅粥。
They're not organised. And as a result,
traffic, congestion, chaos.

309
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:15,840
呵，好笑的是，就在同一周我们刚听闻
Well, it's funny that comes in
the same week that we've heard

310
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:21,320
如今开车的平均耗时
慢了整整16%。
that the average car journey
is now 16% slower.

311
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,400
大家开自己的车跑相同的路程，
It's taking people 16% longer

312
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,280
耗时居然多出了16%。
to make the same journeys in their cars.

313
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:27,760
比四年前还慢？
- 对。我倒觉得这点都不稀奇。
Than it was four years ago?
- Yes. I don't know if that's
a big surprise.

314
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,600
我平时接送孩子上学的路，不在伦敦，
The school run I have to do not in London,

315
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:33,280
是从牛津城外开进牛津市中心，
it's from outside Oxford
into the centre of Oxford,

316
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,160
全英国对汽车“最友好”的城市……
the most car-friendly city in Britain...

317
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,800
好吧行，第二友好的城市。
Well, okay, second most car-friendly.

318
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:41,400
如今18英里的路，要开一个半小时。
That's now 18 miles, an hour and a half.

319
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:43,800
而最有意思的地方在于，
The interesting point being,

320
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:46,400
你们猜车流量到底增加了多少？
how much do you think
the traffic has increased by?

321
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,840
要造成这种局面的车流量。
The volume of traffic to achieve that.

322
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:50,000
通勤时间足足增加了16%。
So, journeys 16% longer.

323
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:52,400
你们觉得马路上到底
多了多少辆车？
How many more cars
do you think there are on the roads?

324
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:55,400
女观众：二。
- 多了百分之二？
WOMAN: Two.
- Two percent more.

325
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:58,840
还是就多了两辆？大蠢蛋！那哪至于啊。
Or two cars? You fool! That wouldn't do it.

326
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:01,280
你们都猜错了。要不要揭晓答案？
You're wrong. Should we say how many more?

327
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,880
我来告诉你们：一辆都没多。
I'm gonna tell you. None.

328
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,520
车流量完全没变，然而
通行时间却慢了那么多。
It's exactly the same and yet
journey times are that much slower.

329
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:07,960
全是拜我们刚才说的
那些破烂事所赐……
- 可不是嘛。
And that's because of
all the stuff we've...
- That's why.

330
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,840
换作以前，那哥们儿在那条道上
起码能开到70英里。
That guy would have
been doing 70 in that lane.

331
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:13,640
现在因为那玩意儿，只能憋屈地开到40。
Now he's having to do 40 because of that.

332
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,920
哟，来车了。
- 嗨。
Ooh, there's something coming.
- Hello.

333
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:19,600
克拉克森：是一辆出租车，
又一辆出租车，还有一辆出租车。
CLARKSON: It's a taxi,
another taxi and another taxi.

334
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:21,280
一口气从希思罗机场开过来三辆。
That's three coming in from Heathrow.

335
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,040
问题就在这儿。
This is the problem.

336
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,360
还有，你们见识过他们搞的
最新公交车站骗局吗？
And now have you see
the latest scam they got with bus stops?

337
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,480
以前路边好歹有个公交停靠港湾，
There used to be a lay-by for buses.

338
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,480
对吧？好让老太太们慢慢上车。
Okay? So that the old ladies could get on.

339
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:34,160
现在可好，他们直接把公交站
往马路中间凸出来建。
Now, they're building
bus stops out into the road.

340
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,480
图什么呢？
- 这是最新的“绝妙主意”，
Why?
- This is the latest idea

341
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,200
因为公交司机老抱怨说
because bus drivers were saying

342
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,880
根本没人给他们让路出站。
that no-one was letting them out.

343
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,920
[笑声]
[LAUGHS]

344
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,280
“呜呜，没人让我出来。”
"Nobody lets me out."

345
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,840
所以现在大家都得干等老太太在那儿磨叽：
So now we have to wait while she dithers.

346
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,120
“哎哟，我的格子买菜小拉车还没提上来呢！”
"Ooh I've got me tartan shopping trolley!"

347
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,680
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

348
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,120
总之。
Anyway.

349
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:51,640
在此之……什么？
- 男观众：你经常坐公交出行是吧？
Before... What?
- MAN: Travel a lot, do you?

350
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:54,360
我经常坐公交……？
- 你觉得呢？
Do I travel a lot on...
- What do you think?

351
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:58,280
[全场大笑]
- 我其实坐过一次公交车。
[ALL LAUGHING]
- I went on a bus once.

352
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:01,000
那年我八岁，恶心透顶。
（另见：Top Gear第36季第13集，1996年11月18日）
I was eight. It was hideous.
(See also: S36E13 of Top Gear, 18/11/1996)

353
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:03,720
言归正传，最近美国那边吵得不可开交，
Anyway, there's been a lot of talk recently

