00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:10,480
就能彻底回本，
you will have recouped the money

737
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:12,040
把当初改装掏的钱全省出来。
you have actually spent on the conversion.

738
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:14,960
太棒了，这叫全赢——我们赢，
环保也赢，皆大欢喜。
Great, so we all win, us,
the environment, everybody's happy.

739
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,080
不过有个问题。
But there is a problem.

740
00:31:16,120 --> 00:31:17,560
燃气之所以这么便宜，
The gas is only so cheap because

741
00:31:17,600 --> 00:31:19,640
纯粹是因为政府冻结了税收
the government has frozen the tax on it

742
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:20,960
来压低价格。
to keep it cheap.

743
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,880
而且他们承诺
这项政策只持续到2004年。
And they have promised
to do that until 2004.

744
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:25,600
那之后呢？
So what happens then?

745
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:28,480
万一他们突然脑子一抽说：
“管他的，咱们还是加点税吧。”
When they suddenly say
"Let's bung some tax on it after all."

746
00:31:28,520 --> 00:31:30,440
他们当年对柴油不就这么干的？
- 没错。
They did it with diesel, didn't they?
- Yeah.

747
00:31:30,480 --> 00:31:31,720
要是他们故技重施怎么办？
What if they do that again?

748
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:32,920
那我们全得傻眼。
We're all stuffed.

749
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,400
我们刚把车改成了烧液化气，
We've converted our cars to run on LPG

750
00:31:34,440 --> 00:31:35,880
转头就得当冤大头掏钱。
and we've got to pay for it.

751
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,320
所以到底要不要改车烧气，
So whether or not
to convert your car to run on gas

752
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:40,240
全取决于一件事。
depends on one thing.

753
00:31:40,280 --> 00:31:42,760
你们信得过政府吗？
Do you trust the government?

754
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:44,000
观众：信不过！
AUDIENCE: No.

755
00:31:44,040 --> 00:31:45,400
可不是嘛，我跟你们讲。
No, I'll tell you what.

756
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,560
我觉得这帮当官的最搞笑的一点，
The funniest thing for me
about the government

757
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:49,560
就是他们最近居然决定，
is that they recently decided to judge

758
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:51,840
要交多少公务车税，
how much company car tax you pay

759
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:55,200
居然取决于你的排气管
喷出了多少二氧化碳。
on how much carbon dioxide
comes out of the back.

760
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,800
简直蠢到家了。
What a stupid thing.

761
00:31:57,840 --> 00:32:00,800
它又不是什么致命毒气。
看到这张图表了吧？
It's not a killer gas.
We've got this chart here, okay?

762
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:04,040
上面清楚地标明了
二氧化碳到底都打哪儿来的。
And this shows where
carbon dioxide comes from.

763
00:32:04,080 --> 00:32:09,320
整整95.5%都来自大自然。
95.5% comes from nature.

764
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:11,160
有人会到处追着农夫收税，
Do they go round taxing farmers

765
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:13,800
就凭他们养了一群牛吗？
for their flocks of cows?

766
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:16,000
埃特纳火山每次喷发，
有人向它收过税吗？
Do they tax Mount Etna
every time it blows up?

767
00:32:16,040 --> 00:32:17,760
简直荒唐透顶。
It's ridiculous.

768
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:20,640
只有这块小小的橙色细条
才是人类折腾出来的。
Only this little orange sliver
here comes from man.

769
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:23,960
而这当中，发电厂占了34%。
And of that, 34% from power stations.

770
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:26,320
全怪那些给电动车充电的人。
People charging up their electric cars.

771
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:30,640
然后还有14%来自日常生活。
And then you've got 14% from domestic use.

772
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:33,880
比如波特顿锅炉，
怎么不干脆把他们税到关门大吉？
Potterton's Boilers,
tax THEM out of business.

773
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:35,160
可看看他们在针对谁，
Look what they're doing

774
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:38,920
因为在那微不足道的一丁点儿里，
because only 13% of that
little tiny bit there

775
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:40,600
只有13%来自汽车。
comes from cars.

776
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:43,520
简直可笑。但既然规矩已经立了，
Ridiculous. But we have the rules

777
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,480
我们《Top Gear》的职责，
and it's our job on Top Gear

778
00:32:45,520 --> 00:32:49,000
就是教大家怎么钻这个空子。
to show you a way round them.

779
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:50,320
[全场大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

780
00:32:50,360 --> 00:32:52,600
这就要请出眼前这位了，瞧好了。
And that's where this comes in, okay?

781
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:58,040
一台莲花Elise，这玩意儿
一加仑油能跑40英里。
A Lotus Elise, now this does
40 miles to the gallon.

782
00:32:58,080 --> 00:33:03,200
整整40英里，而且它在税费档位上
居然跟一台福特嘉年华平起平坐。
Forty, but it's in the same
tax bracket as a Ford Fiesta.

783
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,520
一点不假。
It is.

784
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:09,720
所以，在法律条文上它挑不出半点毛病。
So, it obeys the letter
of the law perfectly.

785
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:12,080
但立法初衷呢？完全没有。
But the spirit? No.

786
00:33:12,120 --> 00:33:13,720
半毛钱都不沾边。
Not even slightly.

787
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,960
克拉克森：这辆当然就是新款Elise，
CLARKSON: This, of course,
is the new Elise,

788
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:30,400
你可以选配普通的1.8升发动机，
which you can have with the normal
1.8 litre-engine

789
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:32,400
改调校、瞎折腾都很容易。
that's easy to tune and tinker with.

790
00:33:32,440 --> 00:33:36,840
但这台111S版本，配的是完全封死的1.8升机头，
But this version, the 111S,
has a sealed-for-life 1.8,

791
00:33:36,880 --> 00:33:41,800
还塞满了各种复杂花哨的玩意儿，
比如可变气门正时。
with all sorts of complicated trickery
like variable valve timing.

792
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:45,160
它能榨出156匹制动马力，
It offers up 156 brake horsepower,

793
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:47,320
零到60英里加速只要5秒，
zero-to-60 in five seconds,

794
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:50,800
极速能飚到132英里每小时。
and a top speed of 132.

795
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:01,720
那问题来了，它怎么会这么省油，
So how come then, it's so economical

796
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:04,040
而且对环境这么友好呢？
and so kind to the environment?

797
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:08,880
究竟是怎么做到的，嗯？怎么可能？
How does it do that, hmm? How?

798
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:13,560
秘诀就在于重量。这车比驾驶员还轻。
The key is weight. This car
weighs less than the driver.

799
00:34:13,600 --> 00:34:16,480
所以根本不需要多少油就能拉着它跑。
So it doesn't need much fuel
to move it around.

800
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:18,480
这么说吧，你根本不需要
Put it like this, you don't need

801
00:34:18,520 --> 00:34:21,120
拿火箭发动机去推一块舒芙蕾。
a rocket motor to move a souffle.

802
00:34:23,240 --> 00:34:25,240
在老款Elise上，莲花从来不给装
Lotus never fitted the old Elise

803
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:26,520
电动车窗。
with electric windows.

804
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:28,640
倒不是因为太贵，
Not because they were too expensive

805
00:34:28,680 --> 00:34:31,520
纯粹是升降电机太沉了。
but because the motors were too heavy.

806
00:34:31,560 --> 00:34:34,280
他们以前连地毯都舍不得铺，可眼前这台，
And they never fitted carpets
either and yet this one,

807
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:36,480
这台居然全铺了威尔顿高级地毯，
this one has the full Wilton

808
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:40,600
甚至还有空调、
CD机，外加真皮内饰。
and air conditioning
and a CD player, and leather.

809
00:34:40,640 --> 00:34:45,720
这么说来，
莲花是不是有点向舒适妥协变质了？
So does this mean, then,
that Lotus has sold out a bit?

810
00:34:51,040 --> 00:34:52,760
并没有。
No.

811
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:56,520
瞧见他们换上的这套新轮圈了吗？
See these new wheels that they've fitted?

812
00:34:56,560 --> 00:34:59,440
精致吧？精巧又轻盈。
Delicate, aren't they? Delicate and light.

813
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,880
确切地说，比老款车上的轮圈
Specifically, six kilograms lighter

814
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:04,480
整整轻了6公斤。
than they used to be on the old car.

815
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:06,760
所以，哪怕塞进了这么多奢华配置，
So, even with all the new luxuries,

816
00:35:06,800 --> 00:35:10,720
整台车加在一块儿
也仅仅只有760公斤。
the whole car in total
only weighs 760 kilograms.

817
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:13,640
差不多也就跟奔驰的一个座椅头枕一样重。
That's about the same
as a Mercedes headrest.

818
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:15,720
再加上后面塞了更强劲的动力，
And with the extra power in the boot,

819
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:17,800
开起来理应更有乐趣才对。
it should be even more fun to drive.

820
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:20,400
爽爆了。
Great.

821
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:29,000
老款Elise曾被无数人誉为
The old Elise was described by many as

822
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:31,000
“全世界操控最佳的汽车”，
"The best-handling car in the world",

823
00:35:31,040 --> 00:35:34,800
而初上手时，
这台新车也同样没让人失望。
and initially,
this doesn't disappoint either.

824
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:38,600
噢，这转向手感
还是一如既往的无可挑剔。
Oh, this steering
is still just as good as ever.

825
00:35:39,520 --> 00:35:42,880
极其细腻，路感丰富得惊人。
It's so delicate, and so much feel.

826
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:44,960
你就算轧死一只昆虫，
You could run over an insect

827
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,920
光凭方向盘传来的路感反馈，
and know just from the messages
coming through the wheel

828
00:35:47,960 --> 00:35:50,440
都能清清楚楚数出它有几条腿。
how many legs it had.

829
00:35:50,480 --> 00:35:52,800
是只甲虫？还是只蜘蛛？
Was it a beetle? Or was it a spider?

830
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:55,120
等等，是蜘蛛。
Hang on, spider.

831
00:35:57,040 --> 00:35:58,400
那真正的操控表现到底如何？
So what about the handling?

832
00:36:00,560 --> 00:36:03,800
噢，推头！严重的推头！
Oh, understeer. Big understeer.

833
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:05,360
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

834
00:36:07,520 --> 00:36:09,680
我知道老款Elise动态极其神经质，
I know the old Elise was very twitchy,

835
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:12,360
把不少人都吓破了胆。
and some people were scared by that.

836
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:14,840
所以他们在这台上换了更窄的前胎，
So they fitted narrower tyres

837
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:17,800
想借此削减车头的抓地力，
on this one to reduce front-end grip,

838
00:36:17,840 --> 00:36:20,400
但依我看，他们根本不是削减，
but I don't think they've reduced it.

839
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:21,640
而是彻底把抓地力给削没了。
They completely removed it.

840
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,360
好了，我们马上要进锤头弯了。
Here we are, coming up
to the Hammerhead now.

841
00:36:23,400 --> 00:36:25,400
好，切入弯心，不给油。
Okay, turn in, no power.

842
00:36:25,440 --> 00:36:28,320
我的天啊。
[轮胎尖叫]
Oh, Lord.
[TYRES SCREECH]

843
00:36:28,360 --> 00:36:31,160
你见过推头推成这样的吗？
Have you ever seen understeer like this?

844
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:34,200
哎呦喂。
Oh, dear.

845
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:41,800
甩了！甩起来了！
Slide! Slide!

846
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:45,200
你要是真发了疯，
一脚把车尾给甩出去，
And if you do go mad
and kick the rear end out,

847
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:48,240
最后就会原地掉头，面朝来时的路。
you end up facing the way you came.

848
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:50,200
陷在一阵浓烟里。
In a cloud of smoke.

849
00:36:57,640 --> 00:36:59,640
所以，就目前摆在眼前的表现来看，
So, on the evidence we've seen so far,

850
00:36:59,680 --> 00:37:02,400
这车可真不怎么样。
not a particularly good car.

851
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,160
但这位是加文·克肖，来自Lotus，
But this is Gavin Kershaw, he's from Lotus

852
00:37:05,200 --> 00:37:08,040
他坚称这车一点问题都没有，
and he says there's nothing
wrong with the car,

853
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:10,680
纯粹是我开车技术的问题。
the problem was my driving.

854
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:13,440
于是他主动提出带我上咱们的赛道跑一圈，
So he offered to take me out on our track

855
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:15,680
亲自示范这车究竟该怎么开。
and show me how it should be done.

856
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,640
所以你是Lotus的首席底盘调校一把手？
So you're the chief chassis man at Lotus?

857
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:24,360
首席底盘工程师之一，没错。
One of the principal chassis
engineers, yes.

858
00:37:24,400 --> 00:37:26,080
而且你住在诺福克。
- 没错。
And you live in Norfolk.
- Yep.

859
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:28,360
那你有女朋友吗？
- 我有个女朋友。
So you got a girlfriend?
- I have got a girlfriend.

860
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:29,640
她有几个轮子？
How many wheels has she got?

861
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:32,800
天哪。
Goodness.

862
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:35,080
好吧，我本来其实是想问她有几条腿来着？
Well, I was going to say
how many legs has she got?

863
00:37:35,120 --> 00:37:37,360
反正都一样。
[两人大笑]
Same thing.
[BOTH LAUGHING]

864
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:41,080
[轮胎尖叫]
[TYRES SCREECH]

865
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:47,920
我刚才怎么就开不出这架势。
I couldn't make it do that.

866
00:37:47,960 --> 00:37:51,520
你是怎么做到的？
它怎么就不推头了？
How are you doing it?
Why doesn't it just understeer?

867
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:54,240
克肖：动作必须极其细腻，这车有点违背物理常识。
KERSHAW: You have to be very
gentle with it. It defies physics.

868
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:55,880
进这个弯道的时候，
Coming down this corner,

869
00:37:55,920 --> 00:38:00,120
踩下刹车，
然后猛打方向入弯再收油。
put on the brakes,
then flick it in and lift.

870
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:03,480
我的天。
God.

871
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:07,440
过这里可不能全油门。
Not flat out through here.

872
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:12,920
你们为什么把它调得
Why've you made it more understeery

873
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:15,160
比老款Elise还容易推头？
than the old Elise?

874
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:17,280
因为我们要卖出三千辆，
Because we're selling 3,000 cars,

875
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:19,720
得照顾到所有水平的驾驶者。
we have to cater for all drivers.

876
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:22,480
我们调校底盘就是为了让你哪怕根本
We make the chassis so if you don't know

877
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:25,080
不会开车，也能玩得转。
how to drive, you can play with it.

878
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,680
克拉克森：我现在真想吐你一身。
CLARKSON: I could vomit on you now.

879
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:31,000
我真的在认真考虑吐你身上。
I'm really considering vomiting on you.

880
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:32,480
[克拉克森呻吟]
[CLARKSON GROANS]

881
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:35,640
我看某些人真是越来越不顺眼了。
I can go off people.

882
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:41,280
我确实挺佩服的，
I'm really quite impressed,

883
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:46,520
但同时也相当郁闷，
凭什么我做不到而你却能做到。
and actually quite depressed at how I
couldn't do that and how you can.

884
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:49,480
我们又要过那个锤头弯了。
We're going round
that Hammerhead corner again.

885
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:52,800
甩尾进弯。继续甩。
Oversteer in. Oversteer.

886
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:55,480
要撞轮胎墙了。
Into the tyres.

887
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:59,280
哥们儿，你刚才离轮胎墙就差那么一丁点。
You were so close to the tyres, man.

888
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:01,600
我们现在能回家了吗？
克肖：行啊。
Can we go home now?
KERSHAW: Yeah.

889
00:39:01,640 --> 00:39:04,240
这么开车可算不上什么体面聪明的举动，对吧？
It's not big nor clever
to drive like that, is it?

890
00:39:04,280 --> 00:39:06,000
姑娘们，这种开法把你们震住了吗？
女观众：震住了。
Are you impressed, girls,
with driving like that?
WOMEN: Yes.

891
00:39:06,040 --> 00:39:09,920
真震住了？好吧，那搬去诺福克郡吧。
他们那儿的人全这么开。
You are? All right. Move to Norfolk, then.
They all do that.

892
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:13,000
但问题是，
我又不住在诺福克。
The thing is, though,
I don't live in Norfolk.

893
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:14,240
我可是有正经生活的人。
I have a life.

894
00:39:14,280 --> 00:39:17,160
所以，如果我要买这么一辆车，
So, how do I kill the understeer

895
00:39:17,200 --> 00:39:18,760
怎么才能解决推头问题？
if I were to buy a car like that?

896
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:20,920
我们可以提供选配的加宽前胎，
We can supply optional bigger front tyres

897
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:22,600
这样就连你开也不会推头了。
so even you won't get understeer.

898
00:39:22,640 --> 00:39:24,840
真的？你们能卖我大号轮胎？
- 没错。
Really, you can sell me big tyres?
- Yes.

899
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:26,760
这就能解决？太妙了。
- 对。
That would solve it? Brilliant.
- Yup.

900
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:29,760
所以我们现在唯一要做的，
So all we need do now is see how fast

901
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:30,680
就是看它绕我们赛道能跑多快。
it goes round our track.

902
00:39:31,640 --> 00:39:33,280
放斯提格！
Unleash the Stig.

903
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:36,360
起步了！
And he's off.

904
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,400
当然，对斯提格来说，转向过度
Of course, for the Stig, oversteer

905
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:40,400
和转向不足根本不是问题。
and understeer are not really the issue.

906
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:44,760
要想做出最快圈速，他必须
走线极其干净利落。
To get the best time, he needs to
keep it nice and tidy.

907
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:47,080
好，现在进入一号弯。
And here we are into the first corner.

908
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:51,440
瞧瞧这个。即使在湿地路况下，
依然丝般顺滑。
Look at that. Even in the wet,
it's as smooth as silk.

909
00:39:51,460 --> 00:39:54,460
♪ 斯潘道芭蕾合唱团 - 《True》 ♪
♪ Spandau Ballet - True ♪

910
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:58,680
看他那副样子，正美滋滋地
享受着Elise的车载音响呢。
Look at him, really enjoying
the Elise's stereo here.

911
00:40:00,560 --> 00:40:03,280
好，现在他来到了锤头弯。
So here he is at the Hammerhead.

912
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:05,000
这个弯角当年是由路特斯设计的。
This corner was designed by Lotus.

913
00:40:05,040 --> 00:40:07,560
Elise过这儿应该很有一套，确实如此。
The Elise should be good
through here, and it is.

914
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,480
完全没有上周本田NSX
None of the slithering about

915
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:12,320
那种滑来滑去的狼狈样。
we had from the Honda NSX last week.

916
00:40:12,340 --> 00:40:19,440
♪ 我买了一张看世界的门票 ♪
♪ 如今我却已归来—— ♪
♪ I bought a ticket to the world, ♪
♪ but now I've come back- ♪

917
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:24,960
说真的，这台车很有希望
刷出一个奇快无比的成绩。
You know, this car is on
for a seriously fast time.

918
00:40:25,000 --> 00:40:26,640
我是说，真的巨快。
I mean really fast.

919
00:40:27,480 --> 00:40:28,880
再瞧瞧斯提格，
And look at The Stig,

920
00:40:28,920 --> 00:40:30,840
他手里的方向盘几乎都不用怎么费劲去救。
he's hardly having to work at that wheel.

921
00:40:30,880 --> 00:40:32,320
开起来太轻松了。
It's all so easy.

922
00:40:32,360 --> 00:40:33,920
只要你懂点门道，
If you know what you're doing,

923
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:38,200
这车的平衡性简直绝了。
this is such a well-balanced car.

924
00:40:38,240 --> 00:40:40,600
于是，连续第五个星期，
So, for the fifth week on the trot,

925
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:42,480
斯提格都得冒雨跑圈。
The Stig had to go round in the rain.

926
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:44,400
但这圈速快得惊人。
But the time was astonishing.

927
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:47,280
1分35秒。
One minute, 35 seconds.

928
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:51,320
这跟法拉利575打了个平手，
That's the same as a Ferrari 575,

929
00:40:51,360 --> 00:40:54,400
而它不过配了台1.8升发动机。
and it only has a 1.8 litre engine.

930
00:40:54,440 --> 00:40:56,920
不过，咱们先别得意忘形。
However, let's not get carried away.

931
00:40:56,960 --> 00:41:00,120
它可不是花钱能买到的……
It is not the most
environmentally friendly car

932
00:41:00,160 --> 00:41:01,560
……最环保的车。
that money can buy.

933
00:41:02,160 --> 00:41:03,880
因为那一辆才是。
Because that is.

934
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,760
杰森、理查德，二位请揭幕。
Jason, Richard, do the honours.

935
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,800
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

936
00:41:08,840 --> 00:41:12,560
这是一台标致607。
This is a Peugeot 607.

937
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:16,320
至于它为什么如此环保，原因很简单。
And the reason why it's so green is simple.

938
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:18,560
它太烂了。烂到令人发指。
It's awful. It's dreadful.

939
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,000
要是你买了这玩意儿，
If you bought one of these,

940
00:41:20,040 --> 00:41:23,320
我保证你绝不会想把它开去任何地方。
I guarantee you'd never drive it anywhere.

941
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:25,280
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

942
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:27,680
好了。现在，又到了请明星……
Right. Now, it's time to put a star

943
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:29,880
……开廉价车的时刻了。
in our reasonably-priced car.

944
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:33,360
他曾105次登上《流行顶峰》（Top of the Pops），
He's been on Top of the Pops 105 times.

945
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:36,080
但今天，他来到了“最高档位”（Top of the Gear）。
But now, he's on Top of the Gear.

946
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:40,080
女士们先生们，
Status Quo乐队的，里克·帕菲特！
Ladies and gentlemen,
from Status Quo, Rick Parfitt.

947
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:41,760
[观众掌声]
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

948
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:50,080
近来可好？请坐。
How are you? Have a seat.

949
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:54,400
说老实话，在咱们环保周这期，
You're not the ideal guest

950
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:56,960
你可算不上是什么理想嘉宾。
to have on in environmental week,
I have to be honest.

951
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,280
对，确实算不上，真不是。
No. Not really, no.

952
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:00,640
昨晚我们在办公室里，翻查了
We went through some of your singles

953
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:02,760
你历年来的各种单曲和热门金曲。
and hits over the years
in the office last night.

954
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:04,640
结果没在任何一首歌里
We didn't find a single environmental lyric

955
00:42:04,680 --> 00:42:06,360
找到哪怕一句关于环保的词。
- 没错，半句都没有。
in any of them.
- No. None at all.

956
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:08,760
净是些情情爱爱还有亲嘴什么的，
It's just about love and stuff like that
and kissing

957
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:11,000
全都是那种傻里傻气的调调，你懂的。
and all that sort of dopey stuff, you know.

958
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:13,400
好吧，可人家卖得好啊。
- 那确实很卖座。
Yeah, well. And it sells.
- It certainly does.

959
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:15,960
呃，新专辑？
- 对。
Erm, new album?
- Yep.

960
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,600
《重度拥堵》（Heavy Traffic）。
- 没错。
Heavy Traffic.
- Yeah.

961
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:20,920
受这玩意儿启发的？
- 名字起得倒挺贴切，不是吗？
Inspired by this?
- Aptly named, isn't it?

962
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:23,400
没，其实完全没受任何启发。
No, it wasn't inspired by anything, really.

963
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:25,720
不过说真的，这事儿简直离大谱，不是吗？
But I mean, this is unbelievable, isn't it?

964
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:28,640
当初刚划出来那会儿，
我记得我当时还在想……
When it first went in,
I remember thinking...

965
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:32,440
那可是进希思罗机场的瓶颈路段。
It's a bottleneck going into Heathrow.

966
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:34,040
通向欧洲最大的城市。
Europe's biggest city.

967
00:42:34,080 --> 00:42:36,440
在那种地方搞这个，硬生生夺走一条车道
To put that in there, to take a lane away

968
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:39,000
从我们手里抢走，我觉得简直无耻透顶。
from us, I think it's disgraceful.

969
00:42:39,040 --> 00:42:40,480
这可是M4高速。
This is the M4.

970
00:42:40,520 --> 00:42:41,920
你在M4高速上也有过惨痛经历，对吧？
You've had some bad times
on the M4, haven't you?

971
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:43,520
我？
- 没错。
Me?
- Yeah.

972
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:46,720
我撞车是在M3高速上，对，是M3。
I had a shunt on the M3, it was. Yeah.

973
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:50,560
是在M3？
- 那次撞车彻底改变了我对开车的看法。
Was the M3?
- It kind changed my whole view
about driving.

974
00:42:50,600 --> 00:42:53,080
打那之后我变得懂事多了，
I kind of became sensible after that

975
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:55,160
现在基本都会老老实实按限速开。
and I kind of stick to the speed limit now.

976
00:42:55,200 --> 00:42:56,840
挺无聊的，你懂的。
- 真的假的？
Bit boring, you know.
- Really?

977
00:42:56,880 --> 00:42:58,240
就像看完摇滚演出后去喝杯茶。
Like a cup of tea after a concert.

978
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:00,520
喝杯茶，然后上床睡觉。
A cup of tea and go to bed.

979
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:03,040
真够“摇滚”的。但我现在确实这样。
Real rock'n'roll. But I do.

980
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:06,960
我现在觉得，
驾照这玩意儿实在太珍贵了。
I feel these days
a license is a precious thing.

981
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:08,200
对我来说绝对如此，
It certainly is to me

982
00:43:08,240 --> 00:43:09,520
我知道对很多人来说也是。
and I know it is to a lot of other people.

983
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:13,320
我可真不想再被吊销驾照了。
And I really don't want to lose it
any more.

984
00:43:13,360 --> 00:43:15,360
我都丢过三次驾照了。
- 三次？！
I've lost it three times.
- Three times?

985
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:18,160
而且每次被吊销的经过都精彩绝伦。
And in great circumstances.

986
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:21,760
真的？有那么精彩？
- 呃，最后那次绝对堪称传奇，没错。
Really? Were they?
- Well, the last one
certainly was, yeah.

987
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:26,520
当时我正以估计120英里的时速
沿着M3高速一路狂飙。
I was doing an estimated
120 mph down the M3.

988
00:43:26,560 --> 00:43:28,000
我其实也不知道具体开了多快，
I don't know what speed I was going

989
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,000
因为当时我其实睡着了。
because I was actually asleep.

990
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:32,080
[全场爆笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

991
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:35,600
你就是在那儿撞烂的？
- 没错，我命大得很。
Is that where you stuffed it?
- Yeah, I was very lucky.

992
00:43:35,640 --> 00:43:37,720
我觉得当时要是开的哪怕比保时捷
I think had it been in anything lesser

993
00:43:37,760 --> 00:43:39,600
稍次一点的车，
than a Porsche,

994
00:43:39,640 --> 00:43:42,640
我今天大概就没命坐在这里了，但我运气极好。
I probably wouldn't be sitting here now,
but I was very lucky.

995
00:43:42,680 --> 00:43:44,720
车子原地打转。当时大概是凌晨四点，
It kind of spun. It was like
4:00 in the morning

996
00:43:44,760 --> 00:43:46,440
所以万幸的是周围没有别人，
and so fortunately nobody else

997
00:43:46,480 --> 00:43:49,000
也没波及到任何人。
was around or involved.

998
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:50,280
但最后我的车冲进了田里，
But I ended up in a field,

999
00:43:50,320 --> 00:43:52,280
而我本人就坐在那儿美滋滋地接着大睡。
and just sat there merrily sleeping.

1000
00:43:52,320 --> 00:43:53,920
[全场爆笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

1001
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:56,440
我压根就没醒过来。
I didn't wake up at all.

1002
00:43:56,480 --> 00:43:59,160
那么，最初究竟是什么
让你迷上保时捷的？
So what was it that first
turned you onto Porsches?

1003
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:01,000
我以前有辆Mini Cooper S，
I had a Mini Cooper S,

1004
00:44:01,040 --> 00:44:04,640
早年间买的，那是我这辈子
最喜欢的车之一。
in the early days which is one
of my all-time favourite cars.

1005
00:44:04,680 --> 00:44:06,440
现在依然是，你知道的，就带双油箱那款。
It still is, you know, with the twin tanks.

1006
00:44:06,480 --> 00:44:07,440
其实我对新款还挺失望的，
I'm really rather brought down actually

1007
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:09,200
就新款，那台新的Cooper S，
with the new one, the new Cooper S

1008
00:44:09,240 --> 00:44:10,520
它居然没配双油箱。
that it hasn't got the twin tanks.

1009
00:44:10,560 --> 00:44:11,720
懂你，就像捷豹也必须得有双油箱才对味。
I know, like Jags should have twin tanks.

1010
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:13,960
完全赞同。要是做成相通油箱就完美了。
I agree. A common tank. It would be great.

1011
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:17,880
话说回来，有回我在A3公路上等红灯，
However, I was sitting on
the lights on the A3,

1012
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:19,520
那时候A3公路上还有红绿灯呢，
when the A3 used to have lights

1013
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:21,800
前面正好是一条笔直的大直道，
and it's a complete straight piece of road,

1014
00:44:21,840 --> 00:44:24,000
我那台Cooper S做过扩缸，
and the Cooper S I'd had it
kind of bored out

1015
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:26,880
削平了缸头，还装了Recaro赛车桶椅，
and shaven and the Recaro racing seat,

1016
00:44:26,920 --> 00:44:29,880
改了直通排气，懂吧，
那简直是件大杀器。
the straight-through, you know,
it was a real tool.

1017
00:44:29,920 --> 00:44:31,800
那天晚上，有个玩意儿慢悠悠停在我旁边，
So this thing pulls up beside me this night

1018
00:44:31,840 --> 00:44:34,840
我当时摩拳擦掌，
就等着绿灯起步烧胎弹射，
and I am really looking forward
to this burn away

1019
00:44:34,880 --> 00:44:37,080
结果一给油，那玩意儿“嗖”的一下就把我甩得没影了，
from the lights and this thing
just went away from me

1020
00:44:37,120 --> 00:44:38,960
我当时完全不知道那是台什么车。
and I had no idea what it was.

1021
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:40,960
后来到了下一个红绿灯路口
我才追上它，
I later found out, I caught it up at
the next set of lights

1022
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:43,560
一看原来是辆保时捷，
我心想：我必须也得整一辆！
and it was a Porsche
and I thought, I've got to have one.

1023
00:44:43,600 --> 00:44:45,240
幸运的是，托大家的福，
And luckily enough
I've been in the position

1024
00:44:45,280 --> 00:44:47,120
我的财力刚好买得起保时捷。
where I can afford a Porsche.

1025
00:44:47,160 --> 00:44:51,560
于是我就买了一辆，打那以后我陆陆续续
买了十辆……十一辆保时捷。
And so I got one and I've had 10,
11 of them since then.

1026
00:44:51,600 --> 00:44:53,200
十一辆保时捷？！
- 对啊。
Eleven Porsches?
- Yeah.

1027
00:44:53,240 --> 00:44:54,680
你现在还在开吗？
Are you still on them now?

1028
00:44:54,720 --> 00:44:57,680
早不开了。因为自从
我出了那次车祸之后，
No I'm not. Because since
I had the accident

1029
00:44:57,720 --> 00:45:00,320
我老妈——愿上帝保佑她，她现在已经过世了——
my mum, bless her, she's passed away now,

1030
00:45:00,360 --> 00:45:02,960
她当时对我说：“看在上帝的份上，
你可别再买保时捷了！”
but she said "For Christ's sake,
don't buy another Porsche,"

1031
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,240
后来我就真没买。
and I haven't.

1032
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:05,400
我再也没买过，
I've never had another one.

1033
00:45:05,440 --> 00:45:07,000
甚至再也没开过。
I've never driven another one.

1034
00:45:07,040 --> 00:45:09,400
到现在得有七八年
没碰过保时捷了。
Seven, eight years now
since I've driven a Porsche.

1035
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:11,520
那她就没劝过你：“你干嘛不把
Didn't she ever say, "Why don't you give up

1036
00:45:11,560 --> 00:45:13,280
酒和那些药给戒了？”
"the booze and the drugs?"

1037
00:45:13,320 --> 00:45:14,760
［全场大笑］
- 因为搞不好那才是
[ALL LAUGHING]
- Because probably that was

1038
00:45:14,800 --> 00:45:17,920
引发车祸的罪魁祸首，而不是车的问题？
causing the accidents more than the car?

1039
00:45:17,960 --> 00:45:20,640
我就随口一说。
- 我妈是个明白人。
Just a thought.
